{
  "name": "SmartCommerce AI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "inputText": "={{ $json.snippet }}",
        "categories": {
          "categories": [
            {
              "category": "Order",
              "description": "whenver email comes with text inside new order seprate it."
            },
            {
              "category": "Inquiry",
              "description": "when emaiil come about inquiry of product or service seprate it to inquiry department."
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "systemPromptTemplate": "You are an email classification assistant for an online store.\n\nClassify each customer email into exactly one category: Order or Inquiry.\n\nORDER:\nThe customer is clearly placing an order or confirming a purchase. Examples:\n- I want to order 2 wireless keyboards.\n- Please place an order for 3 wireless mice.\n- I confirm my purchase of 1 headset.\n\nINQUIRY:\nThe customer is asking questions about products, prices, availability, specifications, delivery, or store information. Examples:\n- What is the price of wireless headphones?\n- Is the iPhone 16 Pro available?\n- I want to buy an iPhone 16 Pro. Can you tell me its price and availability?\n- Do you have gaming keyboards in stock?\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n1. If the customer asks for price, availability, or more information before purchasing, classify as Inquiry.\n2. The words 'buy', 'purchase', or 'order' alone do not automatically mean Order.\n3. Classify as Order only when the customer clearly requests an order to be placed or confirms a purchase.\n4. If an email contains both buying interest and questions about price or availability, classify as Inquiry unless it explicitly asks to place the order now.\n5. Never use information from previous customer emails.\n6. Return only the appropriate category according to the classifier's configured categories."
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.textClassifier",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
